    },
    "q-72912": {
      "dom_id": "step-q72912",
      "name": "Question 8",
      "problem": "Let $R=[2,7]\\times [-5,-4]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}=\\{{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}\\},\\,{P}_{2}=\\{{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}\\},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate the double integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ is a function such that ${m}_{ij}={M}_{ij}=-5$ for all partitions $P$ of $R,$ and ${m}_{ij}$ and ${M}_{ij}$ are the minimum and maximum values of $f$ respectively in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$",
      "worked_solution": "For a function $f(x,y),$ the double integral of $f$ over a rectangular region $R$ is the unique number $I$ (if it exists) such that\n\n$$\nL(f,P)\\le I\\le U(f,P),\n$$\n\nover all partitions $P$ of $R,$ where the lower and upper sums respectively are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{m}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} \\\\ U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{M}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand ${m}_{ij}$ and ${M}_{ij}$ are the minimum and maximum values of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ \n\nNow, since ${m}_{ij}={M}_{ij}=-5,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P)=U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(-5)\\,Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} \\\\  & =-5({\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i})({\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}) \\\\  & =-5(7-2)(-4-(-5)) \\\\  & =-5\\cdot 5\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-25.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\nL(f,P)=-25\\le {∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A\\le -25=U(f,P)\n$$\n\nwhich implies that\n\n$$\n{∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A=-25.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
